. *** Solution No. 2: Not our preference, but here we use "xtreg, fe" which was
>  the command we stated to be going use in our PAP. 
. *However, we realised that we cannot calculate clustered standard errors at t
> he household level since individuals are not perfectly nested in households .
> ..      
. xtset pid counter

Panel variable: pid (unbalanced)
 Time variable: counter, 1 to 10
         Delta: 1 unit

. gen first_hid=hid

. replace first_hid=l.hid if counter==2
(64 real changes made)

. replace first_hid=l2.hid if counter==3
(65 real changes made)

. replace first_hid=l3.hid if counter==4
(58 real changes made)

. replace first_hid=l4.hid if counter==5
(42 real changes made)

. replace first_hid=l5.hid if counter==6
(29 real changes made)

. replace first_hid=l6.hid if counter==7
(20 real changes made)

. replace first_hid=l7.hid if counter==8
(10 real changes made)

. replace first_hid=l8.hid if counter==9
(3 real changes made)

. replace first_hid=l9.hid if counter==10
(3 real changes made)

. 
. xtreg `dep_var' fc##dvs2 `new_varlist', i(pid) fe vce(cluster first_hid) // N
